curl 8.15 turned CURL_NETRC_IGNORED / _OPTIONAL / _REQUIRED from members of the
CURL_NETRC_OPTION enum into plain `long` macros (0L/1L/2L), leaving only
CURL_NETRC_LAST in the enum. Assigning those macros to a CURL_NETRC_OPTION
variable is then an invalid long->enum conversion, so CMake 3.31.6 will not build
against a system curl of that vintage.

CURLOPT_NETRC is a varargs long option, so holding the value in a `long` is both
correct and what curl itself expects; comparisons against the remaining
enumerator still work through the usual integral promotion.

--- a/Source/cmCurl.cxx
+++ b/Source/cmCurl.cxx
@@ -170,7 +170,7 @@
                                  const std::string& netrc_file)
 {
   std::string e;
-  CURL_NETRC_OPTION curl_netrc_level = CURL_NETRC_LAST;
+  long curl_netrc_level = CURL_NETRC_LAST;
   ::CURLcode res;
 
   if (!netrc_level.empty()) {
